  "notes": "HIGH CONFIDENCE — primary-tier (WITS/UN Comtrade). This is India's single largest spice export by value: USD 1.297 BILLION in 2024 across ~537,599 MT. China alone takes ~35% of value. Note the HS nuance: WITS reports under the legacy aggregate 0904.20; current HS2017+ nomenclature splits this into 0904.21 (dried, neither crushed nor ground) and 0904.22 (crushed or ground), so a customs filing should use the split code. Strong candidate for the highest-priority blog cluster (China, Thailand, Indonesia, Sri Lanka, Bangladesh all major)."
